{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1017098-shattered-dreams-is-awesome","id":1017098,"title":"Shattered Dreams is awesome!","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-12-14T09:06:40-08:00","id":1017098,"title":"Shattered Dreams is awesome!","content":"I am still reading Shattered Dreams. I have just finished reading the War of Shame section. I really like this book, even if it is technically non-canon. I intend to treat it as canon unless and until it is preempted by other material in a printed canon book. Even then, I would have to think carefully before I decided which conflicting interpretation to use. One thing I did notice: in the War of Shame section, there is not one single reference to the Yama Kings. Their role as corrupters of the Ten Thousand Immortals has seemingly been taken over by the Kumo (Asian Ananasi). I have no objection to this, but I did find it interesting.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>My name is Colleen. My favorite song is &quot;Wildwood Flower.&quot; My ambition is to write the complete history of the White Wolf/Onyx Path universe.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11905-julianmoon","name":"JulianMoon","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"253"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-12-14T14:18:21-08:00","id":1017311,"title":"","content":"I, for one, am ecstatic you like it! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> The relationship between the Kumo and the Ten-Thousand Immortals is (was?) complicated. The Kumo certainly aided and abetted the Immortal's slide into corruption, but the Immortals would have got there eventually themselves. Absolute Power corrupts absolutely, etc. The Immortals were so far removed from their descendants as to be completely different species (and in my games the Immortals were, in fact, descended from the hominid survivors of the Toba eruption, and thus probably Homo Floriensis (sp?) and definitely not Neanderthal, Cro-Magnon or Denisovan).<br /> <br /> I did seed one possible beginning to the Yama kings in the War of Shame, as corrupt Immortals reign in their own hell-realms created in the aftermath of the Mountain-That-Was-Not's obliteration. Those particularly foul beings may well have been corrupt for millennia, and working to tear down their fellows, and thus could be interpreted as the Yama Kings working to corrupt the Ten-Thousand Immortals prior to the possible Hells even existing as such.<br /> <br /> YMMV, of course. All non-canon, etc. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.dropbox.com/s/ofii86boiyk38ng/DtDRandomForms.zip\" target=\"_blank\">Open the gates of Hell: Random Demon Generator.</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/spreadsheets/d/1X6qQzoAPrSRNzl3cQcMWasoPv3eK56sIlAOTeay61No/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">Gather an army of Rage! Random Garou Generator.</a><br /> Shapeshifting Historian<br /> Writer - Werewolf: the Apocalypse, Werewolf: the Forsaken, Exalted 3e, TC: \u00c6on","edit